IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `mair-dates`

-- Motor Accident Insurance Regulation 2018 (Qld) -- the provisions a claimant meets: the notice of claim (ss 16-19),
-- settlement (s 20), payment of expenses (s 21), information the insurer obtains (s 22), costs when a mandatory final
-- offer is accepted (s 29), examination allowances (s 30) and the gratuitous insurance of motorised mobility devices
-- (s 14).
--
-- The core is seat-neutral: it uses the regulation's own actors and terms ("the claimant", "the insurer", "the
-- commission", "the court", "the public trustee"). Each rule is preceded by the words it encodes. The claimant's
-- questions are in mair-seat.l4.
--
-- Not deposited, and so taken as inputs: the Act's s 100A lower offer limit, upper offer limit and declared costs
-- limit (fixed by the Minister); the Uniform Civil Procedure Rules 1999 schedule 2 item 1 and item 5 costs; the
-- Transport Operations (Road Use Management) Act 1995 meaning of "motorised mobility device"; "adult" and "full
-- capacity".
--
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Motor Accident Insurance Regulation 2018 -- core`

-- An item of a list of requirements, present only when its condition holds.
GIVEN `the condition` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the item`      IS A STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`required if` `the condition` `the item` MEANS
    IF `the condition` THEN JUST `the item` ELSE NOTHING

§§ `s 14 Gratuitous insurance`

-- s 14(1): "For section 23(7) of the Act, motorised mobility devices are a class of vehicles for which gratuitous
-- insurance is provided by the Nominal Defendant." (2): "motorised mobility device see the Transport Operations (Road
-- Use Management) Act 1995, schedule 4" -- a borrowed term, asked as a fact.
-- Another vehicle: s 14 says nothing about it (other classes come from the Act), so NOTHING.
GIVEN `the vehicle is a motorised mobility device` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`gratuitously insured by the Nominal Defendant under s 14` `the vehicle is a motorised mobility device` MEANS
    IF `the vehicle is a motorised mobility device` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

§§ `s 16 Notice of claim -- generally`

-- s 16: "A notice of claim must-- (a) be in a form approved by the commission; and (b) be signed and witnessed as shown
-- in the form; and (c) if the form states that some or all of the information to be provided by the claimant in the
-- notice must be verified by the claimant on oath--contain the form of the oath completed, as shown on the form, by
-- the claimant and a person who is permitted by law to administer the oath."
GIVEN `in the approved form`                      IS A BOOLEAN
      `signed and witnessed as the form shows`    IS A BOOLEAN
      `the form requires an oath`                 IS A BOOLEAN
      `the oath is completed by the claimant and a person permitted to administer it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the notice meets s 16` IF
        `in the approved form`
    AND `signed and witnessed as the form shows`
    AND (    (NOT `the form requires an oath`)
         OR  `the oath is completed by the claimant and a person permitted to administer it`)

§§ `s 17 Statement of information for notice of claim`

-- s 17(3): "For a notice of claim, a disability is significant if-- (a) the disability may be relevant to the
-- assessment of the extent of the injury suffered by the claimant in the accident; or (b) the disability or its
-- symptoms lasted for 4 weeks or more." Schedule 5: "disability includes a personal injury and an illness."
-- 4 weeks is 28 days.
GIVEN `the disability may be relevant to assessing the extent of the injury` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the days the disability or its symptoms lasted`                       IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the disability is significant (s 17(3))` IF
        `the disability may be relevant to assessing the extent of the injury`
    OR  `the days the disability or its symptoms lasted` AT LEAST 28

-- s 17(1) and (2), and s 19: what the notice of claim must include, "to the extent the claimant knows or can reasonably
-- find out the information". Items that apply only in some cases are added when they apply:
-- (a)(iv) the employer's name and address "if the claimant is employed"; (b)(iv) the driver's consumption "if the
-- claimant or injured person was an occupant, but not the driver"; (g) the policy details "if a claim has been made
-- under a policy mentioned in paragraph (f)"; (p) the examination dates and certifying doctor "for a claim other than a
-- derivative claim"; (q) "if the claimant consulted a lawyer"; (r) "if the claimant has retained a law practice".
-- Schedule 5: "derivative claim means a claim based on the death of, or injury to, a person in a motor vehicle
-- accident, other than the claimant."
GIVEN `a derivative claim`                                IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant is employed`                          IS A BOOLEAN
      `the injured person was an occupant but not the driver` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a property damage claim has been made on the vehicle` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant consulted a lawyer`                   IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant retained a law practice`              IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`what the notice of claim must include (ss 17 and 19)` `a derivative claim` `the claimant is employed` `the injured person was an occupant but not the driver` `a property damage claim has been made on the vehicle` `the claimant consulted a lawyer` `the claimant retained a law practice` MEANS
    catMaybes (LIST
        `required if` TRUE "s 17(1)(a)(i)-(iii), (v)-(vii): your full name, address, date of birth, gender, email address, Medicare number, and whether you need an interpreter (and the language)",
        `required if` (NOT `the claimant is employed`) "s 17(1)(a)(iv): your occupation",
        `required if` `the claimant is employed` "s 17(1)(a)(iv): your occupation and your employer's name and address",
        `required if` TRUE "s 17(1)(b)(i)-(iii), (v)-(vii): the date, time and place of the accident; whether the injured person was a driver, passenger or other; any protective device used; how it happened; a diagram of the scene; a diagram of where everyone sat",
        `required if` (NOT `the injured person was an occupant but not the driver`) "s 17(1)(b)(iv): the injured person's alcohol or drug consumption in the 12 hours before the accident",
        `required if` `the injured person was an occupant but not the driver` "s 17(1)(b)(iv): the injured person's, and the driver's, alcohol or drug consumption in the 12 hours before the accident",
        `required if` TRUE "s 17(1)(c)-(f), (h)-(i): who you think caused the accident and why; each vehicle's make, model, type, colour, year and registration; owners' and drivers' contact details; whether a property damage claim was made on the vehicle the injured person was in; witnesses' contact details; the police officer, station and accident report number",
        `required if` `a property damage claim has been made on the vehicle` "s 17(1)(g): the property damage policy's insurer, policy number and claim number",
        `required if` TRUE "s 17(1)(j)-(o): your occupation and income at the accident; your significant disabilities; whether you are, or have applied to be, a participant in the national injury insurance scheme for this injury; your claims for, and amounts received as, damages, compensation or social security benefits for a significant disability",
        `required if` (NOT `a derivative claim`) "s 17(1)(p): the date a doctor first physically examined you for the injury, the date the certifying doctor first did, and the certifying doctor's unique identifier",
        `required if` `the claimant consulted a lawyer` "s 17(1)(q): the date you first consulted a lawyer about claiming",
        `required if` `the claimant retained a law practice` "s 17(1)(r): the name of the law practice you retained and the date you retained it",
        `required if` TRUE "s 17(2)(a): a statement of the nature and extent of your loss, as far as it can be assessed at the date of the notice",
        `required if` TRUE "s 17(2)(b): an offer of settlement (the amount you would accept in full satisfaction), or why you cannot yet make one",
        `required if` TRUE "s 19: written permission for the insurer to have access to, and copy, records about you relevant to the claim held by the bodies s 19 lists")

§§ `s 18 Certificates and identity documents to accompany notice of claim`

-- s 18(1): "A notice of claim must-- (a) if the claim is not a derivative claim--be accompanied by a certificate signed
-- by a doctor stating-- ... (ii) that the doctor physically examined the claimant; ... and (b) if the claim is a
-- derivative claim made by or for the dependants of a person who died as a result of injury received in a motor
-- vehicle accident--be accompanied by a copy of the death certificate."
-- s 18(2)-(3): the claimant's certificate, in the approved form and verified by statutory declaration, stating (a)
-- whether the claimant makes the claim on their own initiative, (b) whether they were approached and solicited or
-- induced, and (c) "if the claimant has retained a law practice", whether the claimant knows if the law practice gave
-- consideration for the referral.
-- s 18(4): "if the claimant is at least 15 years", the identity evidence (see `the s 18(4) answer`).
GIVEN `a derivative claim`                                   IS A BOOLEAN
      `a claim by or for the dependants of a person who died` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant's age in years`                          IS A NUMBER
      `the claimant holds an identity document`              IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant retained a law practice`                 IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`what must accompany the notice of claim (s 18)` `a derivative claim` `a claim by or for the dependants of a person who died` `the claimant's age in years` `the claimant holds an identity document` `the claimant retained a law practice` MEANS
    catMaybes (LIST
        `required if` (NOT `a derivative claim`) "s 18(1)(a): a certificate signed by a doctor who physically examined you, giving the doctor's details, whether you were an existing patient, the injury and its effects on your ability to work, and treatment to date and needed",
        `required if` (`a derivative claim` AND `a claim by or for the dependants of a person who died`) "s 18(1)(b): a copy of the death certificate",
        `required if` TRUE "s 18(2)(a)-(b), (3): your certificate, in the commission's approved form and verified by statutory declaration, stating whether you claim on your own initiative and whether anyone personally approached you and solicited or induced the claim (and if so, who and how)",
        `required if` `the claimant retained a law practice` "s 18(2)(c): in that certificate, whether you know if your law practice gave anyone consideration for referring you",
        `required if` (`the claimant's age in years` AT LEAST 15 AND `the claimant holds an identity document`) "s 18(4)(a): a certified copy of your current identity document",
        `required if` (`the claimant's age in years` AT LEAST 15 AND (NOT `the claimant holds an identity document`)) "s 18(4)(b): a recent certified photograph of you")

-- s 18(5): "identity document, for a claimant, means a document issued by a government that is evidence of the
-- claimant's identity and contains a photograph of the claimant."
GIVEN `issued by a government and evidence of the claimant's identity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `contains a photograph of the claimant`                          IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is an identity document (s 18(5))` IF
        `issued by a government and evidence of the claimant's identity`
    AND `contains a photograph of the claimant`

-- s 18(5): "certified copy, of an identity document, means a copy of the document certified by any of the following
-- persons to be a true copy of the document-- (a) a lawyer; (b) a notary public; (c) a commissioner for declarations;
-- (d) a justice of the peace."
DECLARE `Certifier` IS ONE OF
    `a lawyer`
    `a notary public`
    `a commissioner for declarations`
    `a justice of the peace`
    `someone else, or nobody`

GIVEN `who certified the copy as a true copy` IS A `Certifier`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a certified copy (s 18(5))` IF
    CONSIDER `who certified the copy as a true copy`
    WHEN `someone else, or nobody` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- s 18(5): "recent certified photograph, of a claimant, means a passport-size photograph of the claimant taken within
-- the last 2 years and certified to be a photograph of the claimant by a person who has known the claimant for at least
-- 1 year."
-- READING: "within the last 2 years" is counted back from the day the notice of claim is given, and a photograph taken
-- on the same calendar day 2 years earlier counts; "for at least 1 year" is counted up to the day of the certification.
GIVEN `passport-size`                               IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the photograph was taken`            IS A DATE
      `the day the notice of claim is given`        IS A DATE
      `certified by a person who has known the claimant since` IS A DATE
      `the day it was certified`                    IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a recent certified photograph (s 18(5))` IF
        `passport-size`
    AND `2 years before the notice` `is no later than` `the day the photograph was taken`
    AND `the day the photograph was taken` `is no later than` `the day the notice of claim is given`
    AND `1 year after the certifier came to know the claimant` `is no later than` `the day it was certified`
    WHERE
        `2 years before the notice` MEANS `the day` (0 MINUS 24) `months after` `the day the notice of claim is given`
        `1 year after the certifier came to know the claimant` MEANS `the day` 12 `months after` `certified by a person who has known the claimant since`

DECLARE `Identity evidence answer` IS ONE OF
    `s 18(4) does not apply: the claimant is under 15`
    `met: a certified copy of the claimant's current identity document (s 18(4)(a))`
    `met: a recent certified photograph, as the claimant holds no identity document (s 18(4)(b))`
    `not met: the copy is not certified by a lawyer, notary public, commissioner for declarations or justice of the peace (s 18(5))`
    `not met: the claimant's identity document is not current, and s 18(4)(b) is open only to a claimant who holds no identity document`
    `not met: the photograph is not a recent certified photograph (s 18(5))`

-- s 18(4): "Further, if the claimant is at least 15 years, a notice of claim must be accompanied by-- (a) a certified
-- copy of an identity document for the claimant that is current; or (b) if the claimant does not hold an identity
-- document--a recent certified photograph of the claimant."
-- Finding: the identity document definition has no currency in it, so a claimant whose only identity document has
-- expired "holds an identity document", cannot give (a) (it is not current) and is not let into (b). See NOTES.md.
GIVEN `the claimant's age in years`                 IS A NUMBER
      `the claimant holds an identity document`     IS A BOOLEAN
      `the identity document is current`            IS A BOOLEAN
      `the copy is a certified copy`                IS A BOOLEAN
      `the photograph is a recent certified photograph` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `Identity evidence answer`
`the s 18(4) answer` `the claimant's age in years` `the claimant holds an identity document` `the identity document is current` `the copy is a certified copy` `the photograph is a recent certified photograph` MEANS
    IF `the claimant's age in years` LESS THAN 15
    THEN `s 18(4) does not apply: the claimant is under 15`
    ELSE IF `the claimant holds an identity document`
         THEN IF `the identity document is current`
              THEN IF `the copy is a certified copy`
                   THEN `met: a certified copy of the claimant's current identity document (s 18(4)(a))`
                   ELSE `not met: the copy is not certified by a lawyer, notary public, commissioner for declarations or justice of the peace (s 18(5))`
              ELSE `not met: the claimant's identity document is not current, and s 18(4)(b) is open only to a claimant who holds no identity document`
         ELSE IF `the photograph is a recent certified photograph`
              THEN `met: a recent certified photograph, as the claimant holds no identity document (s 18(4)(b))`
              ELSE `not met: the photograph is not a recent certified photograph (s 18(5))`

-- s 18(5): "consideration means a fee or other benefit but does not include a gift, other than money, or hospitality
-- if the gift or hospitality has a value of $200 or less."
DECLARE `Referral benefit` IS ONE OF
    `money`
    `a gift other than money`
    `hospitality`
    `another fee or benefit`

GIVEN `the kind of benefit`  IS A `Referral benefit`
      `its value in dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is consideration (s 18(5))` IF
    CONSIDER `the kind of benefit`
    WHEN `a gift other than money` THEN `its value in dollars` GREATER THAN 200
    WHEN `hospitality`             THEN `its value in dollars` GREATER THAN 200
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `s 20 Offer of settlement`

-- s 20(1): "An offer of settlement made by an insurer to a claimant must, if the claimant is not represented by a
-- lawyer, be accompanied by an explanatory statement in a form approved by the commission."
GIVEN `the claimant is represented by a lawyer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the insurer's offer must come with an explanatory statement (s 20(1))` IF
    (NOT `the claimant is represented by a lawyer`)

DECLARE `Settlement answer` IS ONE OF
    `s 20(2) does not restrict it: the claimant is an adult of full capacity`
    `yes: the court or the public trustee is satisfied it is in the claimant's best interests and has approved the terms (s 20(2))`
    `no: until the court or the public trustee is satisfied it is in the claimant's best interests and approves the terms (s 20(2))`

-- s 20(2): "If a claimant is not an adult of full capacity, an offer or counteroffer of settlement can not be made or
-- accepted by or for the claimant unless the court or the public trustee-- (a) is satisfied that settlement of the
-- claim on the terms proposed would be in the claimant's best interests; and (b) approves the terms of the offer or
-- counteroffer." The court's or public trustee's satisfaction and approval are judgments, taken as inputs.
GIVEN `the claimant is an adult`                     IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant is of full capacity`             IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court or public trustee is satisfied it is in the claimant's best interests` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court or public trustee approves the terms` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Settlement answer`
`the s 20(2) answer` `the claimant is an adult` `the claimant is of full capacity` `the court or public trustee is satisfied it is in the claimant's best interests` `the court or public trustee approves the terms` MEANS
    IF `the claimant is an adult` AND `the claimant is of full capacity`
    THEN `s 20(2) does not restrict it: the claimant is an adult of full capacity`
    ELSE IF `the court or public trustee is satisfied it is in the claimant's best interests` AND `the court or public trustee approves the terms`
         THEN `yes: the court or the public trustee is satisfied it is in the claimant's best interests and has approved the terms (s 20(2))`
         ELSE `no: until the court or the public trustee is satisfied it is in the claimant's best interests and approves the terms (s 20(2))`

-- s 20(3): "An insurer is entitled to assume that an adult claimant is of full capacity unless-- (a) the claimant's
-- mental incapacity is obvious and should be apparent to the insurer; or (b) the claimant is subject to a protection
-- order under the Public Trustee Act 1978; or (c) the court makes a declaration under subsection (4) in relation to the
-- claimant." A claimant who is not an adult: s 20(3) is silent, so NOTHING.
GIVEN `the claimant is an adult`                                   IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant's mental incapacity is obvious and should be apparent to the insurer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant is subject to a protection order under the Public Trustee Act 1978` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court has declared the claimant under its protection (s 20(4))` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the insurer may assume full capacity (s 20(3))` `the claimant is an adult` `the claimant's mental incapacity is obvious and should be apparent to the insurer` `the claimant is subject to a protection order under the Public Trustee Act 1978` `the court has declared the claimant under its protection (s 20(4))` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the claimant is an adult`)
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST (NOT (    `the claimant's mental incapacity is obvious and should be apparent to the insurer`
                    OR  `the claimant is subject to a protection order under the Public Trustee Act 1978`
                    OR  `the court has declared the claimant under its protection (s 20(4))`))

-- s 20(4): "On application by an interested person, the court may declare a claimant to be under the court's
-- protection in negotiating settlement of the claim if-- (a) the claimant is permanently or intermittently unable to
-- manage the claimant's affairs or to resist undue influence because of physical or mental illness or infirmity, or the
-- influence of drugs; or (b) the claimant is in need of the court's protection for another reason." Whether the court
-- finds (b) is the court's judgment, taken as an input.
GIVEN `an interested person has applied`             IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant is unable to manage their affairs or resist undue influence because of illness, infirmity or drugs` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court finds the claimant needs its protection for another reason` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the court may declare the claimant under its protection (s 20(4))` IF
        `an interested person has applied`
    AND (    `the claimant is unable to manage their affairs or resist undue influence because of illness, infirmity or drugs`
         OR  `the court finds the claimant needs its protection for another reason`)

§§ `s 21 Verification and payment of expenses`

DECLARE `Expense kind` IS ONE OF
    `private hospital, medical and pharmaceutical expenses (Act, s 42)`
    `rehabilitation expenses (Act, s 51)`
    `other expenses`

-- s 21(1): "If a claimant asks an insurer for payment or reimbursement of private hospital, medical and pharmaceutical
-- expenses under section 42 of the Act, or rehabilitation expenses under section 51 of the Act, the request must-- (a)
-- be for a total amount of at least $200; and (b) be accompanied by receipts, unpaid accounts or other appropriate
-- evidence of the expenses." (2): "However, if the claimant expects to make no further request for payment or
-- reimbursement of expenses, the request may be for the outstanding total of the expenses even though the amount is
-- less than $200." Other expenses: s 21 is silent, so NOTHING.
GIVEN `the kind of expenses`                         IS AN `Expense kind`
      `the total amount asked for`                   IS A NUMBER
      `accompanied by receipts, unpaid accounts or other evidence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant expects to make no further request` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the request is for the whole outstanding total` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the request meets s 21` `the kind of expenses` `the total amount asked for` `accompanied by receipts, unpaid accounts or other evidence` `the claimant expects to make no further request` `the request is for the whole outstanding total` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the kind of expenses`
    WHEN `other expenses` THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE JUST (    (    `the total amount asked for` AT LEAST 200
                         OR  (`the claimant expects to make no further request` AND `the request is for the whole outstanding total`))
                    AND `accompanied by receipts, unpaid accounts or other evidence`)

§§ `s 22 Insurer to give information to claimant`

DECLARE `MAIR party` IS ONE OF
    `the insurer`
    `the claimant`

DECLARE `MAIR act` IS ONE OF
    `give the claimant the information`
    `decide to withhold the information` HAS `the days from the decision to 1 month after it` IS A NUMBER
    `inform the commission of the decision and its grounds`
    `ask about the information`

-- s 22(1): "If an insurer obtains information about a claimant under section 19, the insurer must give the information
-- to the claimant within 1 month after obtaining it." (2): "However, an insurer may withhold information from a claimant
-- if the insurer has reasonable grounds to suspect the claimant of fraud." (3): "If an insurer withholds information
-- from a claimant, the insurer must inform the commission of the decision, and of the grounds on which it was made,
-- within 1 month after deciding to withhold the information."
-- The trace starts on the day the insurer obtains the information (day 0) and counts in days; the argument is the
-- number of days to the same day of the next month. Withholding is taken as one way out of the s 22(1) duty, open only
-- on the s 22(2) grounds (an event the trace is given, not a judgment the rule makes); the decision event carries the
-- days from the decision to 1 month after it, and the s 22(3) duty runs that long from the decision.
GIVEN `the days to 1 month after obtaining it` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `MAIR party` `MAIR act`
`s 22 -- the insurer must give the claimant the information within 1 month, unless it withholds it on suspicion of fraud` `the days to 1 month after obtaining it` MEANS
        (PARTY `the insurer`
         MUST  `give the claimant the information`
         WITHIN `the days to 1 month after obtaining it`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST  BREACH BY `the insurer` BECAUSE "s 22(1): the information was not given to the claimant within 1 month after the insurer obtained it")
    ROR
        (PARTY `the insurer`
         MUST  `decide to withhold the information` `the days left`
         WITHIN `the days to 1 month after obtaining it`
         HENCE
             PARTY `the insurer`
             MUST  `inform the commission of the decision and its grounds`
             WITHIN `the days left`
             HENCE FULFILLED
             LEST  BREACH BY `the insurer` BECAUSE "s 22(3): the commission was not told of the decision to withhold within 1 month after it")

-- The last day for the insurer to give the information.
GIVEN `the day the insurer obtained the information` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day to give the claimant the information (s 22(1))` `the day the insurer obtained the information` MEANS
    `the day` 1 `months after` `the day the insurer obtained the information`

§§ `s 29 Costs if mandatory final offer accepted`

-- s 29(1): "For section 51C(4) of the Act, if a mandatory final offer for more than the lower offer limit but not more
-- than the upper offer limit is accepted, the claimant is entitled to payment of costs as follows--"
GIVEN `the amount of the mandatory final offer` IS A NUMBER
      `the lower offer limit`                   IS A NUMBER
      `the upper offer limit`                   IS A NUMBER
      `the offer was accepted`                  IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 29 applies` IF
        `the offer was accepted`
    AND `the amount of the mandatory final offer` GREATER THAN `the lower offer limit`
    AND `the amount of the mandatory final offer` AT MOST `the upper offer limit`

-- s 29(1)(c): "the claimant's costs of legal representation, if any, at the compulsory conference at the rate of $175
-- for the first hour and $150 for every hour after the first and, for a period of less than 1 hour, the relevant
-- proportion of the appropriate hourly rate". Counted in minutes; a part of the first hour at $175 an hour, a part of a
-- later hour at $150 an hour.
GIVEN `the minutes of legal representation at the conference` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the conference representation costs (s 29(1)(c))` `the minutes of legal representation at the conference` MEANS
    IF `the minutes of legal representation at the conference` AT MOST 60
    THEN 175 TIMES (`the minutes of legal representation at the conference` DIVIDED BY 60)
    ELSE 175 PLUS (150 TIMES ((`the minutes of legal representation at the conference` MINUS 60) DIVIDED BY 60))

-- s 29(1): "(a) 100% of item 1 costs; (b) 50% of item 5 costs; (c) [above]; (d) the claimant's costs of an application
-- to the court up to a maximum of $400; (e) reasonable disbursements of which documentary evidence is available."
-- (2): "However, if the amount calculated under subsection (1) is more than the declared costs limit, the claimant's
-- entitlement is limited to the declared costs limit." Item 1 and item 5 costs are "costs allowable under the Uniform
-- Civil Procedure Rules 1999, schedule 2, part 2" items 1 and 5 (s 29(3)), not deposited: inputs. Reasonable
-- disbursements are a judgment, taken at the claimant's figure.
GIVEN `item 1 costs`                                         IS A NUMBER
      `item 5 costs`                                         IS A NUMBER
      `the minutes of legal representation at the conference` IS A NUMBER
      `the costs of an application to the court`             IS A NUMBER
      `reasonable disbursements with documentary evidence`   IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the amount calculated under s 29(1)` `item 1 costs` `item 5 costs` `the minutes of legal representation at the conference` `the costs of an application to the court` `reasonable disbursements with documentary evidence` MEANS
        (`item 1 costs` TIMES (100%))
    PLUS (`item 5 costs` TIMES (50%))
    PLUS (`the conference representation costs (s 29(1)(c))` `the minutes of legal representation at the conference`)
    PLUS (`the smaller of` `the costs of an application to the court` `and` 400)
    PLUS `reasonable disbursements with documentary evidence`

-- The s 29 entitlement. Outside s 29(1)'s band, or when the offer is not accepted, s 29 does not set the costs:
-- NOTHING (fork line 2 in NOTES.md).
GIVEN `the amount of the mandatory final offer` IS A NUMBER
      `the lower offer limit`                   IS A NUMBER
      `the upper offer limit`                   IS A NUMBER
      `the offer was accepted`                  IS A BOOLEAN
      `the declared costs limit`                IS A NUMBER
      `item 1 costs`                            IS A NUMBER
      `item 5 costs`                            IS A NUMBER
      `the minutes of legal representation at the conference` IS A NUMBER
      `the costs of an application to the court` IS A NUMBER
      `reasonable disbursements with documentary evidence` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the s 29 costs entitlement` `the amount of the mandatory final offer` `the lower offer limit` `the upper offer limit` `the offer was accepted` `the declared costs limit` `item 1 costs` `item 5 costs` `the minutes of legal representation at the conference` `the costs of an application to the court` `reasonable disbursements with documentary evidence` MEANS
    IF `s 29 applies` `the amount of the mandatory final offer` `the lower offer limit` `the upper offer limit` `the offer was accepted`
    THEN JUST (`the smaller of` (`the amount calculated under s 29(1)` `item 1 costs` `item 5 costs` `the minutes of legal representation at the conference` `the costs of an application to the court` `reasonable disbursements with documentary evidence`) `and` `the declared costs limit`)
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `s 30 Allowances and expenses for attending examination`

-- s 30: "A person required to attend for examination under part 5B of the Act is entitled to allowances and expenses
-- on the same basis as a witness in a proceeding before the District Court." The District Court scale is borrowed and
-- not deposited. A person not so required: s 30 is silent, so NOTHING.
GIVEN `required to attend for examination under Part 5B of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`entitled to witness allowances and expenses (s 30)` `required to attend for examination under Part 5B of the Act` MEANS
    IF `required to attend for examination under Part 5B of the Act` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING
